nts simple maps for analyzing real communication situations."}, {"id": "6cbefa6e-955f-4b74-a9c9-df85bff90b97", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Major contexts", "children": [{"id": "88da7545-e636-453e-9a97-64a6d0f4c801", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpersonal"}, {"id": "6c5db2e7-76e3-4bf5-b48b-24a494534f67", "type": "concept", "title": "Group and organizational"}, {"id": "d2c9b5ac-2ba6-4acb-83fc-57127e3a0aa4", "type": "concept", "title": "Public"}, {"id": "8a0e7272-9861-44ca-be57-cb91c3bef9d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Mass and digital"}], "description": "The discipline becomes clearer when students can distinguish contexts while noticing how they overlap."}]}, {"id": "fe27c446-0e8b-46e0-b3ff-a0096d5ecbed", "type": "topic", "title": "Perception, Self, Identity, and Meaning-Making", "description": "Explain how people construct meaning through perception, self-concept, identity, culture, and interpretation.", "children": [{"id": "f0cc6afa-9acf-4b6e-bf92-1f0db7138040", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Perception and interpretation", "children": [{"id": "f929ecc0-96d4-4231-8045-b75f6215f7fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Selection"}, {"id": "234235bf-008e-4084-b45c-8e451a5fb3ad", "type": "concept", "title": "Organization"}, {"id": "a8403135-398c-440a-99b3-185924da1323", "type": "concept", "title": "Interpretation"}, {"id": "8320d66c-0367-4a8f-bb57-b30b054a580c", "type": "concept", "title": "Attribution"}], "description": "Perception explains why people can experience the same message differently."}, {"id": "e1d3c885-c69a-4e32-80e5-2af0137161d7", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Self and identity", "children": [{"id": "6f9c39a7-a320-4ebf-94da-108ba46bbafd", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-concept"}, {"id": "426ff508-92d4-44dc-bd1a-8d2a53b78459", "type": "concept", "title": "Social identity"}, {"id": "5f56733d-360f-408c-bc2d-59e13d93ea6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Face"}, {"id": "3952206f-bc00-4ebb-b7fe-0d761ebaef34", "type": "concept", "title": "Impression management"}], "description": "Communication both expresses and shapes who people understand themselves and others to be."}, {"id": "d6407705-a2a9-4d8a-8550-997de87d5bb4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Meaning and social reality", "children": [{"id": "0fe901c6-ca77-4de4-8f24-ce26aef7d349", "type": "concept", "title": "Symbols"}, {"id": "8dcfd73b-084d-4bf1-b774-3955e2e55d59", "type": "concept", "title": "Frames"}, {"id": "4584eb89-44d0-4287-af7d-55b66b48ac0f", "type": "concept", "title": "Norms"}, {"id": "2318b40e-4d60-42c9-854d-2bc9b3525e02", "type": "concept", "title": "Social construction"}], "description": "Students learn that shared meanings, norms, and categories are built through interaction."}]}, {"id": "1f668431-e6b3-4155-842d-ce62738e5fce", "type": "topic", "title": "Verbal Communication, Language, and Framing", "description": "Study how words name reality, coordinate action, shape relationships, and frame public issues.", "children": [{"id": "3a5450a8-cab2-4ae2-b81d-00e8842584bb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language functions", "children": [{"id": "24bcc443-28b7-4838-9ad6-4ae705befcc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Denotation and connotation"}, {"id": "3701348f-953e-4f90-83f5-666ee25b3f67", "type": "concept", "title": "Speech acts"}, {"id": "6ab7ca27-efc3-4a89-9943-43e7eb1853b8", "type": "concept", "title": "Abstraction"}, {"id": "3f9266db-3e73-4115-bcdc-86b75b3adcfe", "type": "concept", "title": "Loaded language"}], "description": "Language does things: it informs, promises, persuades, labels, includes, and excludes."}, {"id": "3f8634c8-352c-4e3b-b305-e411c51cab3e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Framing and narrative", "children": [{"id": "38b893ee-78b1-4863-99da-120d30c2aa24", "type": "concept", "title": "Issue framing"}, {"id": "b0c07ae7-56b7-420c-a7d3-c732be23ea79", "type": "concept", "title": "Metaphor"}, {"id": "b1221e3b-0e71-4ac1-aa7c-59d1ec967390", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative structure"}, {"id": "4d7219ed-d710-4168-b4e5-b45d63f8cdf5", "type": "concept", "title": "Problem definition"}], "description": "Frames and stories shape what audiences notice and what responses seem reasonable."}, {"id": "c6e7a729-072b-417a-a4bc-aad9b4979011", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible language use", "children": [{"id": "c4a43004-ee11-4088-94fa-4d237b967735", "type": "concept", "title": "Plain language"}, {"id": "ba6f8f80-e4fa-4b2e-9304-7d2683092844", "type": "concept", "title": "Inclusive language"}, {"id": "c939d83c-6642-4499-862b-2d98eb096778", "type": "concept", "title": "Credibility"}, {"id": "abaa7997-f69a-44ea-968d-6f222279b801", "type": "concept", "title": "Context sensitivity"}], "description": "Students practice language choices that are clear, accurate, inclusive, and audience-aware."}]}, {"id": "a5233018-0317-44c7-addc-0a1ea4f5e94f", "type": "topic", "title": "Nonverbal Communication and Listening", "description": "Develop skill in interpreting and using nonverbal cues while practicing active, ethical listening.", "children": [{"id": "72747bf1-abc4-4a0e-8518-8a3353d04a99", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nonverbal channels", "children": [{"id": "eebaaa47-8498-498b-a6cc-852bc571cfc3", "type": "concept", "title": "Facial expression"}, {"id": "d17d83fa-e611-4d01-a97f-0f810bd5cc2d", "type": "concept", "title": "Gesture"}, {"id": "4b6a2672-53fa-405a-b511-d18750cb7643", "type": "concept", "title": "Eye contact"}, {"id": "b5625c58-89c0-4119-9881-6765cb696bb0", "type": "concept", "title": "Space and touch"}], "description": "Nonverbal cues help create meaning, regulate interaction, and communicate emotion or status."}, {"id": "9d5e73c9-b495-4748-85b0-c8e10795d041", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Listening as active work", "children": [{"id": "3b4a8990-8afd-4141-8b0e-f8f5b87ed471", "type": "concept", "title": "Attending"}, {"id": "1b9e9ab2-94e5-436e-a13d-e7fd53aa74e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Paraphrasing"}, {"id": "e47a52f9-87c1-4c51-a8ea-d63a6d5e717c", "type": "concept", "title": "Questioning"}, {"id": "7fff3918-1e23-4b17-a611-be17307f9a11", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflective response"}], "description": "Listening is not passive; it is a learned process of attention, interpretation, empathy, and response."}, {"id": "8fb04120-5cc4-4da7-bb65-1f035265547f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Misinterpretation and context", "children": [{"id": "acdf2816-5b45-443e-847f-ec663dc49c03", "type": "concept", "title": "Ambiguity"}, {"id": "98657497-bc27-4080-b2c1-7cdcf7cdfbc0", "type": "concept", "title": "Cultural variation"}, {"id": "2a1ed91b-49e2-4f1e-879a-a587b989ec07", "type": "concept", "title": "Status cues"}, {"id": "f5f5b4dc-bc6b-474b-acc0-358d74601c58", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital nonverbal substitutes"}], "description": "Nonverbal meaning depends heavily on culture, relationship, setting, and power."}]}, {"id": "e4a48738-7b01-4bdd-af7c-8c05b9d69dfd", "type": "topic", "title": "Interpersonal Communication and Relationships", "description": "Understand how communication forms, maintains, repairs, and sometimes harms personal relationships.", "children": [{"id": "2a0ae9af-caaa-4669-8609-2463ead3b7f6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Relationship development", "children": [{"id": "0569785a-df0f-45f4-a582-97f7eafce561", "type": "concept", "title": "Initiating"}, {"id": "52be9e1a-10ca-4e12-9d51-5174f64d2a35", "type": "concept", "title": "Self-disclosure"}, {"id": "925fa324-3fae-4b6f-90c7-316a217c48d5", "type": "concept", "title": "Relational maintenance"}, {"id": "1987c9ea-3270-4d39-bed7-8e41e7474ee9", "type": "concept", "title": "Boundary management"}], "description": "Students learn how relationships begin, deepen, stabilize, and sometimes dissolve through communication."}, {"id": "8baabad6-c2fb-4f49-b380-397b73a05a0a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Conflict and repair", "children": [{"id": "1c3611ef-7eb9-4dd8-b6ff-755227fb2013", "type": "concept", "title": "Conflict styles"}, {"id": "51433598-503b-4448-93f4-97f9b5d62da7", "type": "concept", "title": "Defensiveness"}, 